If your goal is to go from complete beginner to professional Python developer using AI as a tutor, the fastest approach is to combine structured learning with AI-assisted practice.

Phase 1: Learn the Basics (1–3 weeks)

Topics:

Variables and data types
Input/output
Operators
Conditions (if, else)
Loops (for, while)
Functions
Lists, tuples, dictionaries, sets

How to use AI:

Ask: "Explain Python variables like I'm 12 years old."
Ask: "Give me 10 beginner Python exercises with solutions hidden."
Paste your code and ask: "Find bugs without rewriting the whole solution."

Recommended resources:

Python Official Tutorial
freeCodeCamp Python Course

Practice:

Calculator
Number guessing game
Unit converter
To-do list in terminal
Phase 2: Intermediate Python (3–6 weeks)

Topics:

Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
Modules and packages
File handling
Exception handling
List comprehensions
Lambda functions
Virtual environments
Basic testing

Use AI for:

Code reviews
Debugging
Generating practice problems
Explaining difficult concepts

Example prompt:

"Teach me Python OOP through a real-world banking application."

Projects:

Student management system
Expense tracker
Password manager
Library management system
Phase 3: Professional Python Skills (1–2 months)

Topics:

Git and GitHub
APIs
JSON
Databases (SQLite, PostgreSQL)
Web scraping
Logging
Type hints
Design patterns

Resources:

GitHub Docs
FastAPI Documentation

Projects:

Weather app using APIs
